## What Vehicle Types Does California’s Lemon Law Cover?

California’s Lemon Law may apply to various vehicle types when they are purchased new, leased new, or as an eligible CPO. These include:

- Motorhomes

- Recreational Vehicles

Note: Standard used vehicles bought from third-party dealers or with only the remaining original factory warranty are generally not eligible for a manufacturer buyback under recent court rulings.

## What am I entitled to?

California lemon law holds manufacturers to the terms of their warranties, which include:

- Providing adequate repair facilities that are easily accessible to consumers.

- Making a reasonable number of repair attempts (typically two to four times, depending on the defect).

- Addressing situations where the vehicle is out of service for a cumulative total of 30 or more days for repairs.

If your vehicle meets lemon law CA requirements, you are entitled to:

- A full buyback (refund) for the purchase price paid for the vehicle, minus a mileage offset.

- Alternatively, you can request to receive a replacement vehicle or one of similar value.

- All official costs associated with the vehicle (sales tax, registration, etc.).

- Coverage for all incidental expenses (towing fees, cab fares, hotel stays, etc.).

- All [attorney fees](/info/fees) and court costs.

